            487
          ]
        }
      ],
      "trigger": "KILL becomes engaged during SubmissionJournal.before_submit fsync. The new third before_send check raises after the intent is durably stored, before send_raw_transaction is called.",
      "observed": "Fake signing count 1, broadcast attempts 0, one receipt-less processed=False durable record. Two reconciliations refuse receipt not available. Engine.withdraw reconciles first and would encounter this same permanent block.",
      "positive_controls": [
        "Checks 1 and 2 refuse before signing and create no record.",
        "Allowed send signs and sends exactly once, preserving confirmed receipt hash.",
        "An actual ambiguous send attempt remains blocked and is never retried."
      ],
      "fix_requirement": "Record a narrowly proven pre-broadcast cancellation/tombstone when a synchronous gate refusal occurs before the first send attempt. Retain the public hash/intent identity. A crash or any actual/ambiguous broadcast attempt must remain unresolved until venue evidence resolves it.",
